 "answerSources": [], "passages": []}, {"id": "efe9595598b4aff8-p153", "label": "Answers to Quizzes   129", "part": null, "sourceSha256": "efe9595598b4aff807a4037949b246574a32961fe671e7cb18f2e9e7e5313543", "pages": [153, 154], "questions": [{"number": 2, "prompt": "When my dog is tired, she lies on her back.", "sourcePage": 153, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 672}, {"number": 1, "prompt": "According to an old legend, there is treasure buried on that island.", "sourcePage": 154, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 1572, "answer": {"text": "Many people don’t stop to consider how current events affect their", "source": {"id": "offline-efe9595598b4aff807a4", "filename": "The_Blue_Book_of_Grammar_and_Punctuation.pdf", "sha256": "efe9595598b4aff807a4037949b246574a32961fe671e7cb18f2e9e7e5313543", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/efe9595598b4aff807a4037949b246574a32961fe671e7cb18f2e9e7e5313543.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/efe9595598b4aff807a4037949b246574a32961fe671e7cb18f2e9e7e5313543.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}, "page": 155}}], "skills": ["listening", "reading", "writing", "speaking"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-efe9595598b4aff807a4", "filename": "The_Blue_Book_of_Grammar_and_Punctuation.pdf", "sha256": "efe9595598b4aff807a4037949b246574a32961fe671e7cb18f2e9e7e5313543", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/efe9595598b4aff807a4037949b246574a32961fe671e7cb18f2e9e7e5313543.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/efe9595598b4aff807a4037949b246574a32961fe671e7cb18f2e9e7e5313543.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper", "pages": [155]}], "passages": []}, {"id": "efe9595598b4aff8-p156", "label": "The_Blue_Book_of_Grammar_and_Punctuation.pdf", "part": null, "sourceSha256": "efe9595598b4aff807a4037949b246574a32961fe671e7cb18f2e9e7e5313543", "pages": [156, 157], "questions": [{"number": 9, "prompt": "Have you ever watched someone shear a sheep?", "sourcePage": 156, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 131, "answer": {"text": "Jordan did not believe that Serena had embarrassed him unintentionally.", "source": {"id": "offline-efe9595598b4aff807a4", "filename": "The_Blue_Book_of_Grammar_and_Punctuation.pdf", "sha256": "efe9595598b4aff807a4037949b246574a32961fe671e7cb18f2e9e7e5313543", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/efe9595598b4aff807a4037949b246574a32961fe671e7cb18f2e9e7e5313543.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/efe9595598b4aff807a4037949b246574a32961fe671e7cb18f2e9e7e5313543.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}, "page": 158}}, {"number": 18, "prompt": "When we opened the trash can, it reeked of rotten meat.", "sourcePage": 157, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 239}, {"number": 20, "prompt": "When Marie’s plane hadn’t arrived, her mother started wringing her\nhands in worry.\nMore Confusing Words and Homonyms Quiz 3 Answers", "sourcePage": 157, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 393, "answer": {"text": "This is the fifth time that Josef has been called to the principal’s office.", "source": {"id": "offline-efe9595598b4aff807a4", "filename": "The_Blue_Book_of_Grammar_and_Punctuation.pdf", "sha256": "efe9595598b4aff807a4037949b246574a32961fe671e7cb18f2e9e7e5313543", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/efe9595598b4aff807a4037949b246574a32961fe671e7cb18f2e9e7e5313543.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/efe9595598b4aff807a4037949b246574a32961fe671e7cb18f2e9e7e5313543.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}, "page": 158}}, {"number": 5, "prompt": "Whose job is it to clean the kitchen tonight?", "sourcePage": 157, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 883, "answer": {"text": "The boy was struck in the face by the pie as it flew from the girl’s hand.", "source": {"id": "offline-efe9595598b4aff807a4", "filename": "The_Blue_Book_of_Grammar_and_Punctuation.pdf", "sha256": "efe9595598b4aff807a4037949b246574a32961fe671e7cb18f2e9e7e5313543", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/efe9595598b4aff807a4037949b246574a32961fe671e7cb18f2e9e7e5313543.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/efe9595598b4aff807a4037949b246574a32961fe671e7cb18f2e9e7e5313543.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}, "page": 158}}, {"number": 11, "prompt": "When you sand any wood surface, always start with coarse sandpaper.", "sourcePage": 157, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 1408, "answer": {"text": "While singing in the shower, the bar of soap slipped from her hands.", "source": {"id": "offline-efe9595598b4aff807a4", "filename": "The_Blue_Book_of_Grammar_and_Punctuation.pdf", "sha256": "efe9595598b4aff807a4037949b246574a32961fe671e7cb18f2e9e7e5313543", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/efe9595598b4aff807a4037949b246574a32961fe671e7cb18f2e9e7e5313543.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/efe9595598b4aff807a4037949b246574a32961fe671e7cb18f2e9e7e5313543.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}, "page": 158}}], "skills": ["listening", "reading", "writing", "speaking"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-efe9595598b4aff807a4", "filename": "The_Blue_Book_of_Grammar_and_Punctuation.pdf", "sha256": "efe9595598b4aff807a4037949b246574a32961fe671e7cb18f2e9e7e5313543", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/efe9595598b4aff807a4037949b246574a32961fe671e7cb18f2e9e7e5313543.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/efe9595598b4aff807a4037949b246574a32961fe671e7cb18f2e9e7e5313543.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper", "pages": [158, 159]}], "passages": []}, {"id": "efe9595598b4aff8-p160", "label": "The_Blue_Book_of_Grammar_and_Punctuation.pdf", "part": null, "sourceSha256": "efe9595598b4aff807a4037949b246574a32961fe671e7cb18f2e9e7e5313543", "pages": [160, 161, 162], "questions": [{"number": 15, "prompt": "When Toni and he come over, we always have a great time.", "sourcePage": 160, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 1934}, {"number": 18, "prompt": "Who do you think you are to give me advice about dating? (CORRECT)", "sourcePage": 160, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 2190}, {"number": 19, "prompt": "Who makes up these English rules anyway? (CORRECT)", "sourcePage": 161, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 28}, {"number": 20, "prompt": "Who do you think should win?", "sourcePage": 161, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 83}, {"number": 21, "prompt": "Whom are you voting for?", "sourcePage": 161, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 116}, {"number": 26, "prompt": "When you do a job so well, you can expect a raise.", "sourcePage": 161, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 462}, {"number": 28, "prompt": "Harry smells good. What is the aftershave he is wearing? (CORRECT)", "sourcePage": 161, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 578}, {"number": 39, "prompt": "Isn’t it amazing how long that mime can remain completely stationary?\n(CORRECT)", "sourcePage": 161, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 1505}, {"number": 41, "prompt": "How did they manage to serve cold ice cream in the middle of the vast\ndesert?", "sourcePage": 162, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 49}, {"number": 3, "prompt": "‘‘How,’’ I asked, ‘‘can you always be so forgetful?’’", "sourcePage": 162, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 1194}, {"number": 8, "prompt": "Is that book yours?", "sourcePage": 162, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 1643}], "skills": ["listening", "reading", "writing", "speaking"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [], "passages": []}, {"id": "efe9595598b4aff8-p163", "label": "Answers to Quizzes   139", "part": null, "sourceSha256": "efe9595598b4aff807a4037949b246574a32961fe671e7cb18f2e9e7e5313543", "pages": [163, 164], "questions": [{"number": 19, "prompt": "‘‘Would you like to accompany me?’’ he asked.", "sourcePage": 163, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 331}, {"number": 35, "prompt": "‘‘What does it take to become a licensed architect?’’ she asked.", "sourcePage": 163, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 1214}, {"number": 11, "prompt": "Mae said, ‘‘Why don’t you come up and see me sometime?’’", "sourcePage": 164, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 1415}, {"number": 12, "prompt": "You said that I could go, didn’t you? (CORRECT)", "sourcePage": 164, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 1492}, {"number": 14, "prompt": "He seems to be such a lonely, quiet man, doesn’t he?", "sourcePage": 164, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 1641}], "skills": ["listening", "reading", "writing", "speaking"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [], "passages": []}, {"id": "efe9595598b4aff8-p165", "label": "Answers to Quizzes      141", "part": null, "sourceSha256": "efe9595598b4aff807a4037949b246574a32961fe671e7cb18f2e9e7e5313543", "pages": [165, 166, 167], "questions": [{"number": 12, "prompt": "What a delicious, appetizing meal! (CORRECT)", "sourcePage": 165, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 775}, {"number": 7, "prompt": "Did you, John, eat my cake?", "sourcePage": 166, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 2102}, {"number": 8, "prompt": "Did John eat my cake? (CORRECT)", "sourcePage": 166, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 2150}, {"number": 9, "prompt": "Did his friend John eat my cake? (CORRECT)", "sourcePage": 166, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 2202}, {"number": 10, "prompt": "Did John, his friend, eat the cake?", "sourcePage": 167, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 28}, {"number": 3, "prompt": "‘‘Is it almost over?’’ he asked.", "sourcePage": 167, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 1596}, {"number": 5, "prompt": "The song asks, ‘‘Would you like to swing on a star?’’", "sourcePage": 167, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 1703}], "skills": ["listening", "reading", "writing", "speaking"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [], "passages": []}, {"id": "efe9595598b4aff8-p168", "label": "144   The Blue Book of Grammar and Punctuation", "part": null, "sourceSha256": "efe9595598b4aff807a4037949b246574a32961fe671e7cb18f2e9e7e5313543", "pages": [168], "questions": [{"number": 9, "prompt": "‘‘May I have a rain check on that lunch?’’ I asked.", "sourcePage": 168, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 49}, {"number": 11, "prompt": "Bernard said, ‘‘Waldo asked, ‘Who took my pencil sharpener?’’’", "sourcePage": 168, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 295}, {"number": 12, "prompt": "‘‘May I see your I.D. card?’’ the clerk asked.", "sourcePage": 168, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 378}, {"number": 3, "prompt": "Sandi asked, ‘‘Did Jeri say, ‘I am pregnant’?’’", "sourcePage": 168, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 693}, {"number": 6, "prompt": "Did he ask, ‘‘Where are my keys?’’", "sourcePage": 168, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 896}], "skills": ["listening", "reading", "writing", "speaking"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-efe9595598b4aff807a4", "filename": "The_Blue_Book_of_Grammar_and_Punctuation.pdf", "sha256": "efe9595598b4aff807a4037949b246574a32961fe671e7cb18f2e9e7e5313543", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/efe9595598b4aff807a4037949b246574a32961fe671e7cb18f2e9e7e5313543.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/efe9595598b4aff807a4037949b246574a32961fe671e7cb18f2e9e7e5313543.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper", "pages": [169, 170, 171, 172, 173, 174, 175]}], "passages": []}, {"id": "efe9595598b4aff8-p176", "label": "The_Blue_Book_of_Grammar_and_Punctuation.pdf", "part": null, "sourceSha256": "efe9595598b4aff807a4037949b246574a32961fe671e7cb18f2e9e7e5313543", "pages": [176, 177], "questions": [{"number": 25, "prompt": "Jan asked, ‘‘What did Joe mean when he said, ‘I will see you later’?’’", "sourcePage": 176, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 765}, {"number": 26, "prompt": "When I noticed that our dog cut its paw, I called the veterinarian right\naway.", "sourcePage": 176, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 856}, {"number": 37, "prompt": "When Wendy asked her mother about this marriage, Ilse (her mother)\nwas hesitant to discuss any details. (CORRECT OR use commas instead\nof parentheses.)", "sourcePage": 176, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 2148}, {"number": 39, "prompt": "‘‘Do you understand her need for privacy?’’ Wendy asked her husband.", "sourcePage": 177, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 26}], "skills": ["listening", "reading", "writing", "speaking"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [], "passages": []}]}
